  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The design and siting&nbsp;of the porch fails to reflect the design of the&nbsp;original dwellinghouse. It has resulted in the loss of a key architectural feature of the Becontree Estate through the infilling of the shared recessed porch.&nbsp; It fails to appear&nbsp;subordinate and sympathetic to the original dwelling.&nbsp; It presents an obstruction to the right of way and access to the rest of the shared entrance. This is detrimental to the character of the dwellinghouse and is at odds with the appearance and character of the Becontree Estate.&nbsp;The proposal would therefore be contrary to the following policies which seek to ensure that developments are sympathetic to local character and historic distinctiveness:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December, 2024)Policy HC1 of the London Plan (March 2021)The Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012) Policies SPP6, SP2, DMD1, DMD4&nbsp;and DMD5 of The Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September, 2024)"
  ],
